# Cloudflare Pages header rules. Vite copies everything in public/ into dist/
# untouched, and Pages reads this file from the deployment root. Rules combine
# rather than override, so /assets/* also receives the /* headers below.
#
# Vite fingerprints everything under /assets/, so those filenames only ever
# name one build and can be cached forever. index.html must not be: it is the
# thing that points at the new hashes, so a stale copy pins a visitor to the
# previous deploy. Pages already serves it `max-age=0, must-revalidate` by
# default, which is what we want, so it is deliberately left alone here.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The app ships nothing off-origin of its own: no API, no analytics bundled
# into the build, no font or stylesheet from a CDN. That is what makes a strict
# policy possible without an 'unsafe-inline' escape hatch, and it is worth
# keeping that way. Adding a dependency to the build means amending this line,
# and that friction is the point.
#
# The one exception is not ours to remove. Web Analytics is enabled on the
# awknaust.me zone with auto_install, so Cloudflare injects a beacon <script>
# into every HTML response at the edge, for browser-like requests only — a
# plain curl will not show it. That injection happens whether or not this file
# allows it; all a narrow script-src bought was a CSP violation on every page
# load and roughly a tenth of the traffic actually being recorded. So the
# choice here is to allow it or to turn auto_install off in the dashboard, not
# to have no beacon by omission.
#
# script-src names the host with no path. Cloudflare serves the beacon from a
# versioned URL (/beacon.min.js/v4513226...), and a source expression whose
# path has no trailing slash must match the path exactly — so the
# .../beacon.min.js that Cloudflare's own CSP documentation suggests would
# block the very script it is meant to admit. That advice is written for the
# hand-pasted snippet, which does use the bare URL.
#
# connect-src stays 'self' and needs nothing added: under auto_install the
# beacon reports to /cdn-cgi/rum on this origin. Only the manually embedded
# snippet posts to cloudflareinsights.com, and this site does not use it.
#
# data: is for images only, and covers exactly one thing: the SVG chevron
# Bootstrap inlines into its select background. object-src, base-uri and
# form-action are shut off outright — nothing here embeds plugins, rewrites
# the document base, or submits a form.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
